  "content": {
    "id": "p29-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "$f(x)=(x-1)^2-3$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p29-q4-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the largest domain containing $x=3$ such that the inverse is defined.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x\\geq1$.",
          "worked": "The turning point is $(1,-3)$. The branch containing $x=3$ is strictly increasing for $x\\geq1$.\n\nThe largest domain is $[1,\\infty)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p29-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "State the domain and range of $f^{-1}(x)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Domain: $[-3,\\infty)$. Range: $[1,\\infty)$.",
          "worked": "On the restricted domain, $f$ has domain $[1,\\infty)$ and range $[-3,\\infty)$. Interchange these for the inverse.\n\nDomain of $f^{-1}$: $[-3,\\infty)$.\n\nRange of $f^{-1}$: $[1,\\infty)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p29-q4-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Sketch the graph of $y=f(x)$ with the restricted domain and $y=f^{-1}(x)$ on the same axes.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=(x-1)^2-3$, $x\\geq1$, and $y=1+\\sqrt{x+3}$, $x\\geq-3$; reflected in $y=x$. Filled endpoints: $(1,-3)$ and $(-3,1)$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=(x-1)^2-3,\\quad x\\geq1\\\\x&=(y-1)^2-3,\\quad y\\geq1\\\\(y-1)^2&=x+3\\\\y-1&=\\sqrt{x+3}\\\\y&=1+\\sqrt{x+3},\\quad x\\geq-3\\end{align*}$$\n\nUse the positive square root because $y\\geq1$. Reflect the restricted parabola in $y=x$. Its filled endpoint $(1,-3)$ reflects to $(-3,1)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
              "id": "p29-q4-c-answer-graph",
              "role": "solution",
              "format": "tikz",
              "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"graph\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[{\"name\":\"functionBlue\",\"hex\":\"268CFF\",\"reason\":\"original function and its equation label\"},{\"name\":\"inverseRed\",\"hex\":\"EF6068\",\"reason\":\"inverse function and its equation label\"}],\"reference\":\"source page 29, p29-q4-c-answer-graph\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.6cm,y=0.6cm,font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont,>=stealth]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\definecolor{functionBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}\n\\definecolor{inverseRed}{HTML}{EF6068}\n\\path[use as bounding box] (-4.8,-4.4) rectangle (5.2,5.3);\n\\draw[black,line width=0.4pt,dashed] (-4.4,-4.4)--(4.8,4.8);\n\\draw[black,line width=0.5pt,->] (-4.6,0)--(4.9,0);\n\\draw[black,line width=0.5pt,->] (0,-4.2)--(0,5.0);\n\\node[black,below] at (4.8,0) {$x$};\n\\node[black,right] at (0,4.9) {$y$};\n\\draw[functionBlue,line width=0.8pt,->] plot[domain=1:3.828427,samples=90] (\\x,{(\\x-1)^2-3});\n\\draw[inverseRed,line width=0.8pt,->] plot[domain=1:3.828427,samples=90] ({(\\x-1)^2-3},\\x);\n\\fill[functionBlue] (1,-3) circle[radius=1.6pt];\n\\fill[inverseRed] (-3,1) circle[radius=1.6pt];\n\\node[black,below right] at (1,-3) {$(1,-3)$};\n\\node[black,below right] at (-3,1) {$(-3,1)$};\n\\node[functionBlue] at (3.0,-1.7) {$y=f(x)$};\n\\node[inverseRed] at (-2.1,3.8) {$y=f^{-1}(x)$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
              "src": null,
